  <h2>What thermography shows</h2>
  <p>An infrared camera displays apparent surface temperature differences. In buildings, those patterns can reveal air leakage, missing or compressed insulation, and thermal bridging that aren't visible to the eye.</p>
  <p>Active thermography applies a controlled stimulus, such as a pressure difference across the envelope, so these defects show up more clearly in the images.</p>

  <h2>Who it's for</h2>
  <p>Builders, architects, engineering firms, home designers, and homeowners.</p>

